From: Codex <codex@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] xmllite: accept XmlReaderProperty_RandomAccess

Purpose: let Windows 7's shell32 read its libraries (*.library-ms).
Windows behavior: IXmlReader::SetProperty(XmlReaderProperty_RandomAccess)
succeeds; Windows 7's shell32 sets it before reading a library.
Wine before: the property was not implemented (E_NOTIMPL), and shell32
gave up on the library: IShellLibrary::GetIcon failed and the library had
no folders; the folder windows showed every library with the generic
library icon instead of Documents', Pictures', Videos' and Music's.
Change: store the property and return it; the reader keeps the current
element's attributes either way.
Evidence: IShellLibrary of Documents.library-ms gives "imageres.dll,-1002"
and two folders, as on Windows 7; the navigation pane's icons match it.
Scope: all xmllite readers.
---
 dlls/xmllite/reader.c | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/dlls/xmllite/reader.c b/dlls/xmllite/reader.c
index b4acab2..71dee22 100644
--- a/dlls/xmllite/reader.c
+++ b/dlls/xmllite/reader.c
@@ -280,6 +280,7 @@ typedef struct
     strval strvalues[StringValue_Last];
     UINT depth;
     UINT max_depth;
+    BOOL random_access;
     BOOL is_empty_element;
     struct element empty_element; /* used for empty elements without end tag <a />,
                                      and to keep <?xml reader position */
@@ -2823,6 +2824,9 @@ static HRESULT WINAPI xmlreader_GetProperty(IXmlReader* iface, UINT property, LO
         case XmlReaderProperty_MaxElementDepth:
             *value = This->max_depth;
             break;
+        case XmlReaderProperty_RandomAccess:
+            *value = This->random_access;
+            break;
         default:
             FIXME("Unimplemented property (%u)\n", property);
             return E_NOTIMPL;
@@ -2862,6 +2866,11 @@ static HRESULT WINAPI xmlreader_SetProperty(IXmlReader* iface, UINT property, LO
         case XmlReaderProperty_MaxElementDepth:
             This->max_depth = value;
             break;
+        case XmlReaderProperty_RandomAccess:
+            /* the reader keeps the attributes of the current element in any case
+             * (Windows 7's shell32 asks for it to read its libraries) */
+            This->random_access = !!value;
+            break;
         default:
             FIXME("Unimplemented property (%u)\n", property);
             return E_NOTIMPL;
